    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always seen math as a tool, not a subject I’m naturally good at. My vocational diploma taught me practical skills, and I’ve used math in baking—measuring ingredients, scaling recipes. I don’t love it like biology or philosophy, but I find value in its logic and structure. It’s not emotional, but it’s useful.",
